<title>FRANCE: Court objects to Swissair restructure in.</title>
<headline>Court objects to Swissair restructure in.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Paris court turned down a plan by Swissair to restructure its French activities, cut 66 jobs and reduce wages by 4.5 percent, a judicial source said on Monday.</p>
<p>The source said Judge Catherine Taillandier ruled last Thursday that the plan was &quot;irregular,&quot; its job reclassification measures were too vague, and it did not take into account voluntary departures that may be provoked by the wage cuts.</p>
<p>The plan, announced late last year, envisages a spinoff of the cargo activities and sub-contracting of freight activities. The plan was challenged by the staff works council.</p>
<p>The Swiss airline may present a new restructuring plan, but may not in the meantime lay off workers.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
